OL,3,GNEWSABonnybridge couple lose 'angel's
OL,4,Ashare' fungus claim against Diageo
OL,5,
OL,6,FA couple who claimed that the "angel's
OL,7,Fshare" from a whisky bond had blighted
OL,8,Ftheir property have lost their
OL,9,Flong-running case against major drinks
OL,10,Ffirm Diageo.
OL,12,FThomas and Gail Chalmers claimed that
OL,13,Fthe vapour caused damage to outdoor
OL,14,Ffurniture and their house in
OL,15,FBonnybridge, near Falkirk.
OL,17,FThe couple brought a claim for #40,000
OL,18,Fcompensation against the company,
OL,19,Fmaintaining that blackening in and
OL,20,Faround their property required cleaning
OL,21,Fand was "unsightly and depressing".
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,426,420,260,160,0,100
